§ `Section 1427 -- the civil penalty`

-- Only the Attorney General may sue, and only "where a large frontier developer ...
-- fails to report an incident as required by section fourteen hundred twenty-two"
-- (F1). Section 1422(3) puts the reporting duty on every frontier developer, but the
-- article states no penalty for one that is not large; section 1424 keeps duties under
-- other law, none of which is encoded. The amount is "not to exceed one million
-- dollars for a first violation" and "not to exceed three million dollars per
-- subsequent violation", "determined based on the severity of the violation": no
-- minimum is stated, and the article does not say how violations are counted or what
-- makes one "subsequent" (F19). There is no private right of action (section 1427(2)).
-- "fails to report an incident as required by section 1422" plainly reaches the
-- 72-hour report of (3)(a). Whether it reaches the 24-hour "disclose" of (3)(b) is not
-- plain, so that answer says so (F18).
-- src:393 | 7 § 1427. Violations. 1. The attorney general may bring a civil action
-- src:394 | 8 to recover a civil penalty in an amount not to exceed one million
-- src:395 | 9 dollars for a first violation and in an amount not to exceed three
-- src:396 | 10 million dollars per subsequent violation, determined based on the sever-
-- src:397 | 11 ity of the violation where a large frontier developer fails to publish
-- src:398 | 12 or transmit a compliant document required to be published or transmitted
-- src:399 | 13 under this article, makes a statement in violation of subdivision four
-- src:400 | 14 of section fourteen hundred twenty-one of this article, fails to report
-- src:401 | 15 an incident as required by section fourteen hundred twenty-two of this
-- src:402 | 16 article, or fails to comply with its own frontier AI framework.
-- src:403 | 17 2. Nothing in this article shall be construed to establish, authorize
-- src:404 | 18 or create a private right of action associated with violations of this
-- src:405 | 19 article.
@ref Gen. Bus. Law § 1427(1), (2) (src:393-405)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most for a first violation, in dollars` MEANS 1000000

@ref Gen. Bus. Law § 1427(1) (src:393-402)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most for each subsequent violation, in dollars` MEANS 3000000

@ref Gen. Bus. Law § 1427(1) (src:393-402)
DECLARE `what I can be made to pay for the failure` IS ONE OF
    `no civil penalty under section 1427, because I am not a large frontier developer`
    `a civil penalty that only the Attorney General may recover in a civil action` HAS
        `the most for this violation` IS A NUMBER
    `a civil penalty only if section 1427 reaches a failure to disclose within 24 hours, and then only the Attorney General may recover it` HAS
        `the most for this violation, on that reading` IS A NUMBER

@ref Gen. Bus. Law § 1427(1) (src:393-402)
GIVEN `this is my first violation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most for this violation` `this is my first violation` MEANS
    IF `this is my first violation`
    THEN `the most for a first violation, in dollars`
    ELSE `the most for each subsequent violation, in dollars`

@ref Gen. Bus. Law § 1427(1) (src:393-402)
GIVEN m IS A `me and my model`
      f IS A `a failure of mine`
      `this is my first violation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `what I can be made to pay for the failure`
`what I can be made to pay under section 1427` m f `this is my first violation` MEANS
    IF (NOT `I am a large frontier developer` m)
    THEN `no civil penalty under section 1427, because I am not a large frontier developer`
    ELSE
        CONSIDER f
        WHEN `I failed to report a critical safety incident to the office within 72 hours`
            THEN `a civil penalty that only the Attorney General may recover in a civil action` (`the most for this violation` `this is my first violation`)
        WHEN `I failed to disclose an imminent-risk incident within 24 hours`
            THEN `a civil penalty only if section 1427 reaches a failure to disclose within 24 hours, and then only the Attorney General may recover it` (`the most for this violation` `this is my first violation`)

§ `Section 1428(5) -- the office's penalty for a missing disclosure statement`

-- Not a reporting penalty, but one the same developer meets. "If any person develops,
-- deploys, or operates a large frontier model in part in New York state without a
-- current disclosure filed with the office ... submits false information ... or fails
-- to timely pay any assessment", the office "may, after notice and hearing", levy $1,000
-- for each day it fails to file or to correct false information, and an amount equal to
-- the assessments owed. "Large frontier model" is not defined in section 1420 (F20).
-- The days and the assessments owed are facts the developer states; the answer is the
-- most the office may levy under (5)(a) and (b), "in addition to any other penalty".
-- src:446 | 3 5. If any person develops, deploys, or operates a large frontier model
-- src:447 | 4 in part in New York state without a current disclosure filed with the
-- src:448 | 5 office as required by this section, submits false information in its
-- src:449 | 6 disclosure or fails to timely pay any assessment required by this arti-
-- src:450 | 7 cle, in addition to any other penalty or liability that may be imposed
-- src:451 | 8 under this article, the office may, after notice and hearing, levy civil
-- src:452 | 9 penalties, fees, and costs as follows:
-- src:453 | 10 (a) a civil penalty of one thousand dollars for each day the entity
-- src:454 | 11 fails to file a disclosure as required by this section or fails to
-- src:455 | 12 correct false information; and
-- src:456 | 13 (b) an amount equal to the assessments owed.
@ref Gen. Bus. Law § 1428(5) (src:446-456)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the office's penalty per day, in dollars` MEANS 1000

@ref Gen. Bus. Law § 1428(5) (src:446-456)
GIVEN `days without a disclosure, or without correcting false information` IS A NUMBER
      `assessments owed, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most the office may levy under section 1428(5)` `days without a disclosure, or without correcting false information` `assessments owed, in dollars` MEANS
      `days without a disclosure, or without correcting false information` TIMES `the office's penalty per day, in dollars`
    PLUS `assessments owed, in dollars`
